PulseShader - provenance
===========================

This project is derived from Valve's Source SDK and from thexa4/source-pbr, so
it is governed by the Source 1 SDK License: free distribution of source and
binaries is permitted, commercial use is not. That term follows the code by
derivation and applies whether or not a license file ships alongside it.

Chain of derivation
-------------------

  Valve Corporation - Source SDK
    -> ValveSoftware/source-sdk-2013 (Source 1 SDK License)
       -> thexa4/source-pbr, branch feature/pbr-base
          - carried no license of its own; its LICENSE and README were the
            Valve Source 1 SDK License verbatim
          -> sdk/valve-stdshaders/  (8 HLSL headers, copied verbatim at commit
             b8c4b76; unmodified Valve code, redistributed with this repo)
          -> src/shaders/  (formerly our fork of thexa4's shaders; the BRDF
             was rewritten from scratch against the OpenPBR Surface spec and
             no thexa4 code remains, but the derivation is real history)

  Valve Corporation - Alien Swarm SDK (Source 1 SDK License)
    -> src/sdk_override/  (modified copies of SDK headers, corrected to match
       the interface layouts L4D2 actually ships)

Our own work
------------

Written for this project and not derived from Valve or thexa4 code:

  src/pulse_shaderdll.cpp        engine-facing shader DLL entry point
  src/shaders/pulse_shader_convars.cpp   shared shader ConVar definitions
  src/basevsshader_impl.cpp      the three CBaseVSShader methods we need
                                 (bodies are Valve's, from the Alien Swarm SDK)
  src/log.cpp, src/log.h         load-time tracing
  tools/vcspack.py               .fxc -> VCS v6 packer
  tools/mdmp.py, disasm.py, argcount.py   ABI recovery tooling

Note that sdk/valve-stdshaders/ IS redistributed - those 8 headers live in this
repository rather than being fetched at build time, so the Source 1 SDK License
applies to them directly.
